{
  "chapter": "first-agent/first-tools",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "One tool use is a round trip, not a function call: two model requests, and the second",
    "resends everything the first one sent.",
    "The model has no memory of asking. The assistant turn is echoed back verbatim, tool_use",
    "blocks included, because the request is the memory.",
    "Results are matched by toolUseId. Every issued id gets exactly one result, including the",
    "ones that failed — a missing result for an issued id is a malformed conversation.",
    "A failing tool returns a result with isError true and text the model can act on. It does",
    "not throw, and it is never dropped.",
    "Every result for a turn goes back in ONE user message. Splitting them teaches the model",
    "to stop asking for parallel calls.",
    "This handles exactly one round of tool use. If the model asks again after seeing the",
    "result, nothing is listening — that is the `if` that the next chapter turns into a `while`."
  ],
  "catalogue": [
    { "name": "get_order", "argument": "orderId" },
    { "name": "get_account", "argument": "accountId" },
    { "name": "search_policies", "argument": "query" },
    { "name": "query_warehouse", "argument": "question" }
